$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":10},"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"difficulty","role":"img","aria-label":"Schwierigkeit 1 von 3","style":{"margin":0},"children":[["$","span","1",{"className":"on"}],["$","span","2",{"className":""}],["$","span","3",{"className":""}]]}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"0.85rem","fontWeight":800,"color":"var(--muted)"},"children":"Easy"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"fun-fact-box","children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.3rem"},"aria-hidden":"true","children":"!"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Fun fact:"}]," ","„Brontosaurus“ bedeutet „Donner-Echse“ – ein Name, der von seiner enormen Größe inspiriert ist!"]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"margin":"20px 0 16px"},"children":null}],"$L10","$L11",["$","$L12",null,{"title":"Brontosaurus Punkt-zu-Punkt Ausmalbild - Kostenloses PDF","imageUrl":"/images/brontosaurus-puzzle.webp","compact":true}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"0.8rem","color":"var(--muted)","marginTop":10,"lineHeight":1.5},"children":"No sign-up needed. Opens as a PDF. Print on US Letter (8.5 × 11 inch) or A4 paper. Free for home and classroom use."}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/de/dinosaurs/","style":{"display":"inline-flex","alignItems":"center","gap":6,"marginTop":18,"fontWeight":800,"color":"#d94f70","textDecoration":"none"},"children":"Dinosaurs"}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"dot-guide","className":"section","style":{"paddingTop":0,"maxWidth":800,"margin":"0 auto","padding":"0 24px 48px"},"children":[["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem)","marginBottom":12},"children":["Brontosaurus"," ",""]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--muted)","lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":28},"dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"Welcome to one of the most loveable dinosaur Rätsel in the whole collection! The Brontosaurus — whose name means \"thunder lizard\" — was one of the biggest creatures ever to walk our planet. Grab a pencil, find Punkt number one, and let's bring this gentle giant back to life, one line at a time!"}}],[["$","div","1–8",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["1–8"," — ","Der Leiter"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Start at Punkt 1 and verbinde through to Punkt 8 to trace the Brontosaurus's surprisingly small, wedge-shaped head. Children practise short, careful pencil strokes and gentle curved lines here — a lovely way to build early Stiftkontrolle before tackling bigger shapes."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Der Brontosaurus hatte stiftartige Zähne, die ausschließlich dazu dienten, Blätter von den Zweigen abzureißen, nicht zum Kauen. Er verschlang Pflanzen im Ganzen und überließ die harte Arbeit seinem riesigen Magen – eigentlich ein ziemlich cleveres System!"]}]]}]]}],["$","div","9–18",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["9–18"," — ","Der Langhals"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Now here comes the showstopper. Verbinde Punkte 9 through 18 to draw that famously long, sweeping neck that curves gracefully upward. This is a brilliant section for practising smooth, flowing lines — Kinder discover that longer curves need more patience and a steadier hand."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Der Hals des Brontosaurus war bis zu 20 Fuß lang – das entspricht in etwa der Höhe eines zweistöckigen Hauses! Wissenschaftler gehen heute davon aus, dass er sich hauptsächlich von Pflanzen in niedriger bis mittlerer Höhe ernährte, anstatt wie eine Giraffe den Kopf in die Baumkronen zu strecken."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","19–32",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["19–32"," — ","Der Körper"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Continue from Punkt 19 all the way to Punkt 32 to fill out the Brontosaurus's massive, barrel-shaped torso. This longest section of the Rätsel is great for building concentration and stamina — Kinder learn to keep going even when the task feels big. Sound familiar?"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Der Brontosaurus wog zwischen 15 und 17 Tonnen – mehr als drei afrikanische Elefanten zusammen. Trotz dieser außergewöhnlichen Größe war er ein reiner Pflanzenfresser, völlig harmlos und wollte wahrscheinlich einfach nur ein ruhiges Leben inmitten der Farne führen."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","33–42",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["33–42"," — ","Die Beine"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Trace Punkte 33 to 42 to form the four thick, column-like legs. Children begin to notice symmetry and how an animal's body is balanced from side to side. Drawing parallel shapes is a real skill, and this section gives little hands plenty of practice."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Der Brontosaurus lief auf den Zehenspitzen – ein bisschen wie eine Ballerina auf vier Beinen! Unter jedem Fuß befand sich ein dickes, fleischiges Polster, das wie ein natürliches Kissen wirkte und jeden donnernden Schritt durch die Landschaft des Jura abfederte."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","43–50",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingInlineStart":16,"borderInlineStart":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["43–50"," — ","Der Schwanz"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Finish the Rätsel by connecting Punkte 43 through 50 to draw the long, tapering tail sweeping out behind the dinosaur. The tail balanced the heavy neck and gave the Brontosaurus its graceful, almost boat-like silhouette. Children practise gradually narrowing their line — a satisfying way to end."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Paläontologen glauben, dass der Brontosaurus seinen Schwanz wie eine Peitsche knallen lassen konnte, wobei ein Geräusch entstand, das so laut war wie ein Donnerschlag! Nicht schlecht für einen sanften Riesen, der den größten Teil seine